==============================================================================
3. No zero of M_phi on the critical line (analyticity + fine grid)
==============================================================================
  B(a+1/2-it,b+1) = Gamma(z)Gamma(w)/Gamma(z+w),  z=a+1/2-it, w=b+1, z+w=a+b+3/2-it.
  Gamma has no zeros; Re z, Re w, Re(z+w) > 0 for a,b > 0, so no Gamma pole.
  Hence |M_phi(1/2+it)| > 0 for ALL real t (for any theta).

  Numerical confirmation on a fine grid over [0,200] (step 0.01, 20001 points):

      a     b           smallest |M|       at t  #points > min   monotone
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
      1     3         3.748078971e-9      200.0          20001        yes
    [PASS] a=1, b=3: no zero on grid, grid min > 0, |M| decreasing in t: grid min = 3.748079e-9 > 0 at t=200.0; 0 non-monotone steps
    0.5     2         2.499562577e-7      200.0          20001        yes
    [PASS] a=0.5, b=2: no zero on grid, grid min > 0, |M| decreasing in t: grid min = 2.4995626e-7 > 0 at t=200.0; 0 non-monotone steps
      2     4         7.48958142e-11      200.0          20001        yes
    [PASS] a=2, b=4: no zero on grid, grid min > 0, |M| decreasing in t: grid min = 7.4895814e-11 > 0 at t=200.0; 0 non-monotone steps
      1     6        5.613082776e-14      200.0          20001        yes
    [PASS] a=1, b=6: no zero on grid, grid min > 0, |M| decreasing in t: grid min = 5.6130828e-14 > 0 at t=200.0; 0 non-monotone steps
    [PASS] inf over all of R equals 0 (power decay): |M(1/2+i*1e6)|(a=1,b=3) = 6.0e-24 -> 0; so the 'c>0 for all t' branch is FALSE

