==============================================================================
7. The honest N-t trade-off (multiplicative in |M_phi|)
==============================================================================
  error(t,N) ~ sqrt(N) |M_phi(1/2+it)|, so accuracy eps is reachable iff
      N <= (eps/|M_phi|)^2 .

  Example: phi(u) = u(1-u)^3 (a=1,b=3), Gamma(b+1) = 6.0

           t        |M(1/2+it)|      N_max(eps=1e-3)      N_max(eps=1e-6)       t^{2(b+1)}
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        10.0    0.0004954723292            4.0734387         4.0734387e-6           1.0e+8
        50.0     9.521830961e-7            1102958.2            1.1029582      3.90625e+13
       200.0     3.748078971e-9        7.1184024e+10            71184.024         2.56e+18
      1000.0    5.999877002e-12        2.7778917e+16        2.7778917e+10          1.0e+24
     10000.0     5.99999877e-16        2.7777789e+24        2.7777789e+18          1.0e+32

  Power-law form with gamma_w = Gamma(b+1) and eps fixed:
      N_max(t) ~ (eps/gamma_w)^2 t^{2(b+1)}   (polynomial gain in t),
      t_max(N) ~ (gamma_w sqrt(N)/eps)^{1/(b+1)} .

  Fit of d log N_max / d log t over [1e3, 1e5]: 7.99999513134 ; predicted 2(b+1) = 8 ; |error| = 4.869e-6
  Ratio check: N_max(40000)/N_max(10000) = 65535.9748096 ; 4^{2(b+1)} = 65536.0 ; rel.dev = 3.844e-7
    [PASS] N_max exponent == 2(b+1) (fit |error| < 1e-4; ratio rel.dev < 1e-5): fitted slope 7.999995131 vs 8; ratio rel.dev 3.844e-7

==============================================================================
8. Resolution of OP-14
==============================================================================
  (1) IDENTICALLY ZERO IS IMPOSSIBLE.  For every nonzero phi the Mellin
      transform M_phi(s) is a Laplace/Mellin transform; if it vanished on the
      line Re s = 1/2 it would vanish identically (analytic continuation) and
      injectivity would force phi = 0.  For the family e^{i theta}u^a(1-u)^b
      this is visible directly: M_phi = e^{i theta}B(a+1/2-it,b+1) and the Beta
      function is a ratio of Gamma values, none of which vanishes on the line.
  (2) NO POSITIVE LOWER BOUND ON ALL OF R.  |M_phi(1/2+it)| ~ Gamma(b+1)|t|^{-(b+1)}
      -> 0, so inf_{t in R} |M_phi| = 0; the 'c > 0 for all t' branch is FALSE.
  (3) WINDOW BRANCH ACHIEVED.  Finite windows [0,T] have a positive minimum; the
      clean weight phi(u)=u(1-u)^3 (theta=0, a=1, b=3) has
      inf_{[0,50]} |M_phi| = 9.521830961e-7 <= 1e-6, and the smallest
      admissible power is b* = 2.98160366189 (at a = 1).
  (4) HONEST TRADE-OFF.  error ~ sqrt(N)|M_phi(1/2+it)|: multiplicative in
      |M_phi|, giving N <= eps^2/|M_phi|^2, i.e. N_max ~ t^{2(b+1)}.  The sqrt(N)
      is never removed; only the constant is improved, by a power of t.

